    (9, None, '\'Forgive me, I will fix everything today.\' "Prosti", \'forgive me\', fits a friend; to the chef, the cooks said prostite. "Ispravlyu", \'I will fix\', comes from pravyy, right, so it means \'make right\'.'),
    (10, None, '\'Never poke your nose into my business again!\' "Lezt\'" means to climb or crawl, and ne lez\' v is \'don\'t poke into\'. Dela, \'affairs\', is plural, the way Russians talk about someone\'s business.'),
